1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
97% accurate. Still confidently wrong.
A real model. A measurable failure.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:10,000
This held-out image is a 3.
The neural network predicts 3 with 60.7% confidence.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Add simulated input noise: it predicts 8 with 96.1% confidence.
This selected example shows that confidence is not correctness.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Across all 275 held-out images, accuracy drops
from 97.45% on clean inputs to 90.18% with simulated noise.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:31,000
EvalDelta blocks the degraded comparison.
A clean-vs-clean control passes.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Actual inference. Reproducible evidence.
53 tests passed locally across both projects.

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Confidence is not correctness. Test the failure cases.
Code: github.com/brohum10/selective-ml and brohum10/evaldelta.
